IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg6-as-made`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg7-1999`

-- Tests of the Dealers chain deposited on 2026-11-04 (Part 3 of the follow-up): S 185/2003 (the Dealers Regulations 2003 as made), S 48/2004, S 593/2004, and S 362/2001 (the amendment of Rg 7).
-- Every expected value is read from the deposited text named beside it, not from the L4.  These are tests of meaning; the evaluation differential is a separate file (sgta-tests-eval-1999-2024.l4).

§ `Rg 6 as made: S 185/2003 reg 1 (in operation 2nd April 2003) and reg 26 (Rg 7 revoked)`
-- TA1999-RG6-S185-2003.txt: reg 1 "shall come into operation on 2nd April 2003"; reg 26 "The Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) are revoked."
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 as made reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 2 April 2003)` (Date 1 4 2003))
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 2 April 2003)` (Date 2 4 2003)
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made reg 1: the Regulations are in operation on the date (from 2 April 2003)` (Date 4 11 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 as made reg 26: the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) are revoked on the date` (Date 1 4 2003))
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made reg 26: the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) are revoked on the date` (Date 2 4 2003)

§ `Rg 6 as made against the 2004 Revised Edition: which regulations read the same`
-- Same words: regs 2, 4 to 8, 11 to 25 and four Schedules; differ: regs 1, 3, 9, 10, 26 and the Second Schedule (a word-by-word comparison with TA1999-RG6-GAZ-RevEd2004.txt, run by script and checked here on the regulations whose differences the amending instruments state).
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "2" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "22" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "25" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "First Schedule" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "Fifth Schedule" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "1" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "3" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "9" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "10" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "26" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "Second Schedule" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "27" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): the words of the regulation are those of the 2004 Revised Edition` "Sixth Schedule" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): how the words of the regulation differ from the 2004 Revised Edition` "2" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): how the words of the regulation differ from the 2004 Revised Edition` "26" EQUALS JUST "regulation 26 revokes the Telecommunication (Dealers) Regulations (Rg 7) and is omitted from the Revised Edition"
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): how the words of the regulation differ from the 2004 Revised Edition` "9" EQUALS JUST "as made 'renewal fee of $400'; S 48/2004 regulation 2 substitutes '$250', which the Revised Edition prints"
#ASSERT `Rg 6 as made (S 185/2003): how the words of the regulation differ from the 2004 Revised Edition` "10" EQUALS JUST "as made paragraph (1)(a) and (b) read '$400'; S 48/2004 regulation 3 substitutes '$250' in each, which the Revised Edition prints"

§ `S 48/2004: regs 9 and 10(1), $400 to $250, in operation 3rd February 2004`
-- TA1999-RG6-S48-2004.txt: reg 1 "shall come into operation on 3rd February 2004"; reg 2 "Regulation 9 ... is amended by deleting '$400' and substituting '$250'"; reg 3 the same for reg 10(1)(a) and (b).
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 S 48/2004 reg 1: the amendment is in operation on the date (from 3 February 2004)` (Date 2 2 2004))
#ASSERT `Rg 6 S 48/2004 reg 1: the amendment is in operation on the date (from 3 February 2004)` (Date 3 2 2004)
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 1 4 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 2 4 2003) (Date 1 4 2003) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 2 4 2003) (Date 2 4 2003) EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 2 2 2004) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 3 2 2004) (Date 2 2 2004) EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 3 2 2004) (Date 3 2 2004) EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 31 12 2004) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `Rg 6 regs 9 and 10(1): the Dealer's Individual Licence renewal fee and annual fee in dollars, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `S 593/2004: Second Schedule paragraph 5, in operation 1st October 2004`
-- TA1999-RG6-S593-2004.txt: reg 1 "shall come into operation on 1st October 2004"; reg 2 deletes paragraph 5 of the Second Schedule and substitutes a paragraph with (a) alter, delete or remove, (b) insert or duplicate "any identification code or number", and (2) SIM cards.
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 S 593/2004 reg 1: the amendment is in operation on the date (from 1 October 2004)` (Date 30 9 2004))
#ASSERT `Rg 6 S 593/2004 reg 1: the amendment is in operation on the date (from 1 October 2004)` (Date 1 10 2004)
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as made: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as made: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as made: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as made: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as substituted by S 593/2004: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as substituted by S 593/2004: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as substituted by S 593/2004: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5 as substituted by S 593/2004: the Class Licensee contravenes the condition` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5(2) as substituted by S 593/2004: the card is "telecommunication equipment" for the paragraph` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5(2) as substituted by S 593/2004: the card is "telecommunication equipment" for the paragraph` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5: the words, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 1 4 2003) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5: the words, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 1 1 2005) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5: the words, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 30 9 2004) (Date 4 11 2026) EQUALS JUST "5. A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale, or use any device or equipment which can be used to alter, delete or remove the ESN, MIN or PIN number of any registered telecommunication equipment or to insert or duplicate the ESN, MIN or PIN number of any registered telecommunication equipment in any unregistered telecommunication equipment."
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5: the words, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 1 10 2004) (Date 26 9 2004) EQUALS JUST "5. A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale, or use any device or equipment which can be used to alter, delete or remove the ESN, MIN or PIN number of any registered telecommunication equipment or to insert or duplicate the ESN, MIN or PIN number of any registered telecommunication equipment in any unregistered telecommunication equipment."
#ASSERT `Rg 6 Second Schedule paragraph 5: the words, for the conduct day, as read on the reading day (2 April 2003 to 31 December 2004)` (Date 1 10 2004) (Date 27 9 2004) EQUALS JUST "5.-(1) A Class Licensee shall not have in his possession for sale, hire or use any device or equipment which can be used (a) to alter, delete or remove any identification code or number of any telecommunication equipment which can be used to obtain any telecommunication services from telecommunication licensees; or (b) to insert or duplicate any identification code or number of such telecommunication equipment in any other telecommunication equipment. (2) For the purposes of this paragraph, telecommunication equipment includes subscriber identification module (‘‘SIM’’) cards."

§ `S 362/2001 amending Rg 7: in operation 1st August 2001 (reg 4(a) deemed from 21st January 2000)`
-- TA1999-DEAL99-S362-2001.txt: reg 1(1) "with the exception of regulation 4 (a), come into operation on 1st August 2001"; reg 1(2) "Regulation 4 (a) shall be deemed to have come into operation on 21st January 2000."
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 S 362/2001 reg 1: the amendment other than reg 4(a) is in operation on the date (from 1 August 2001)` (Date 31 7 2001))
#ASSERT `Rg 7 S 362/2001 reg 1: the amendment other than reg 4(a) is in operation on the date (from 1 August 2001)` (Date 1 8 2001)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 S 362/2001 reg 1(2): reg 4(a) is deemed to have come into operation on the date (from 21 January 2000)` (Date 20 1 2000))
#ASSERT `Rg 7 S 362/2001 reg 1(2): reg 4(a) is deemed to have come into operation on the date (from 21 January 2000)` (Date 21 1 2000)

§ `S 362/2001 reg 2: Rg 7 reg 15 (inspection of the licence)`
-- Reg 15 as substituted: the holder permits an authorised officer ... to inspect his licence or, if it is not immediately available, requires its production within a reasonable period at the office of the Authority or a police station named by the police officer.
#ASSERT `Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001: the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence is meeting the regulation` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001: the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence is meeting the regulation` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001: the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence is meeting the regulation` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001: the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence is meeting the regulation` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Rg 7 reg 15 as substituted by S 362/2001: the holder of a Dealer's Individual Licence is meeting the regulation` FALSE TRUE TRUE)

§ `S 362/2001 reg 3: Rg 7 reg 32 (offence), and the version rule`
-- Reg 32 as substituted: "Any person who contravenes regulation 4 (1) or (4), 6 (2), 12 (2), 14, 15, 17, 18, 19 or 20 (3) or (4) shall be guilty of an offence."  Reg 32 as in the 1999 Edition: "Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with any of the provisions of these Regulations shall be guilty of an offence."
